HIGAKI, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, RYUTA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUKI, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, TSUKASA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical filter comprises a transparent support and a filter layer. The filter layer has an absorption peak in the wavelength range of 620 from 560 nm, and the full width at half maximum of the absorption peak ranges from 5 to 50 nm. This optical filter adequately absorbs undue light in an image display device (particularly, a plasma display panel).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon cette invention, un filtre optique comprend un support transparent et une couche filtrante. La couche filtrante possède une crête d'absorption dans une gamme de largeurs d'onde entre 620 et 560 nm, la largeur maximale de la crête semi-maximale étant comprise entre 5 et 50 nm. Ce filtre optique absorbe de façon adéquate la lumière indésirable dans un dispositif d'affichage d'images (notamment dans un écran plasma).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>